# fr15_log_format_invalid.txtar — FR-15: unknown --log-format value exits 1
# immediately with a flag.invalid error, before any file IO.
#
# GIVEN --log-format=invalid (unrecognised value),
# WHEN nesdit parses flags,
# THEN:
#   - exit code is 1 immediately.
#   - stdout is empty.
#   - stderr contains a flag.invalid event.
#   - no file IO occurs (the nonexistent file argument is never read).
#
# The file argument is deliberately nonexistent to prove the rejection
# happens at flag-parse time (before any IO). If the flag were validated
# at IO time, we would see an io.read error first; instead we see flag.invalid.

! nesdit nonexistent.json --query '.' --log-format=invalid
! stdout .
stderr 'flag\.invalid'
! stderr 'io\.read'
! stderr 'nonexistent'
